Theorem RL-21: no thread boundary makes all values Confined

  Preconditions:
    - Whole-program analysis proves no spawn, channel transfer, foreign export,
      or other thread-boundary capability.
    - The proof is stronger than per-value uncertainty.

  Soundness property:
    Forall Locality L and local crossing flag X:

      (P1) programThreadReachability(true, L, X) = confined.

      (P2) P1 includes Locality.Unknown.

    Physical planners remain free to select any capability satisfying confined.

  Proof obligation:
    Exhaustive Locality x local-signal enumeration under the program proof.

    Part (P1/P2) - whole-program grid:
      every Locality with crossing=false -> confined
      every Locality with crossing=true -> confined
      Coverage gate: all Locality x local-signal cases.

    Engines dispatched:
      case_analysis (PRIMARY - section_08::verify_rl21_no_thread_boundary;
        no_thread_boundary_all_confined)
      rc_counting (SECONDARY - gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL row)
      refinement (SECONDARY - gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL row)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_08 case_analysis engine discharges RL-21 because a whole-program no-thread-boundary proof freezes every Locality case as ThreadReachability.confined
